    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.indentscope\n\n### Description\n\nhttps://github.com/OXY2DEV/helpview.nvim/issues/9\r\n\r\nHi! For some context, please do refer to this issue I was trying to debug and the plugin author suggested that it was an issue related to mini.indentscope. Just wanted to see if something can be done about this.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.11.0-dev-632+g33464189b\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\r\nvim.env.LAZY_STDPATH = \".repro\"\r\nload(vim.fn.system(\"curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/folke/lazy.nvim/main/bootstrap.lua\"))()\r\nrequire(\"lazy.minit\").repro({\r\n\tspec = {\r\n\t\t\"echasnovski/mini.indentscope\",\r\n\t\t\"echasnovski/mini.icons\",\r\n\t\t\"nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter\",\r\n\t\t\"folke/tokyonight.nvim\",\r\n\t\t\"OXY2DEV/helpview.nvim\",\r\n\t\t\"OXY2DEV/markview.nvim\",\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n\r\nrequire(\"mini.icons\").setup({\r\n\tlsp = {\r\n\t\tollama = { glyph = \"\", hl = \"MiniIconsGreen\" },\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\nMiniIcons.mock_nvim_web_devicons()\r\nrequire(\"mini.indentscope\").setup({\r\n\tsymbol = \"│\",\r\n\tdraw = {\r\n\t\tdelay = 0,\r\n\t\tanimation = require(\"mini.indentscope\").gen_animation.none(),\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n\r\nrequire(\"nvim-treesitter.configs\").setup({\r\n\tensure_installed = {\r\n\t\t\"vim\",\r\n\t\t\"vimdoc\",\r\n\t},\r\n\tsync_install = false,\r\n\tauto_install = true,\r\n\thighlight = {\r\n\t\tenable = true,\r\n\t\tadditional_vim_regex_highlighting = false,\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\nrequire(\"helpview\").setup()\r\nrequire(\"markview\").setup()\r\nrequire(\"tokyonight\").setup()\r\nvim.cmd.colorscheme(\"tokyonight\")\r\n```\r\nMinimal configuration to reproduce the issue.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nmini.indentscope does not disrupt extmarks.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nIt disrupts extmarks.",
