            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is not a 'mini.indentscope' related issue per se. Here is a reproduction steps without it:\r\n\r\n- 'init.lua':\r\n    ```lua\r\n    vim.env.LAZY_STDPATH = \".repro\"\r\n    load(vim.fn.system(\"curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/folke/lazy.nvim/main/bootstrap.lua\"))()\r\n    require(\"lazy.minit\").repro({\r\n      spec = {\r\n        \"OXY2DEV/helpview.nvim\",\r\n      },\r\n    })\r\n\r\n    require(\"helpview\").setup()\r\n\r\n    local ns_id = vim.api.nvim_create_namespace(\"test\")\r\n    _G.place_nine_extmarks = function()\r\n      local extmark_opts = {\r\n        hl_mode = \"combine\",\r\n        priority = 2,\r\n        right_gravity = false,\r\n        virt_text = { { \"╎\", \"String\" } },\r\n        virt_text_win_col = 0,\r\n        virt_text_pos = \"overlay\",\r\n      }\r\n      local cur_line = vim.fn.line(\".\")\r\n      for i = 1, 9 do\r\n        pcall(vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark, 0, ns_id, cur_line + i - 1, 0, extmark_opts)\r\n      end\r\n    end\r\n    ```\r\n- Open with that 'init.lua'.\r\n- `:h feedkeys()`. Center the screen so that `extendnew()` line is visible. For example, with `<C-w>ozz`. \r\n- `:lua _G.place_nine_extmarks()`. See that the line \"Like |extend()|\" below `extendnew(expr1, ...)` changes how it looks.\r\n\r\nClosing as not an issue with 'mini.indentscope'.",
